| Building blocks hub builders | `$lib/listings/utils/createBuildingBlocksSeoSchema.ts` | same pattern |

Hub loads (`loadPlaybooksHubPage.server.ts`, `loadBuildingBlocksHubPage.server.ts`) compose builders with `createJsonLdGraph` + `filterNonEmptyJsonLdNodes`. Paginate hub grids in the server load (`parseHubListPagination`, `paginateHubList` from `$lib/listings/utils/hubListPagination.ts`); pass `totalCount` and `listOffset` into item-list builders so `numberOfItems` and `ListItem.position` match the full filtered set, not only the current page slice.

## Reference graph shapes

| Route type | Typical `@graph` nodes |
| --- | --- |
| **Landing** | `WebSite` + `Organization` + `FAQPage` + `VideoObject` + `WebPage` (`#pricing` offers) |
| **About** | `AboutPage` + `Organization` |
| **Pricing** | `WebPage` (paid tiers + self-host `$0` `Offer` list) + `FAQPage` |
| **Hub** | `CollectionPage` + `ItemList` (+ optional `FAQPage`) |
| **Channel / agent detail** | `WebPage` + `SoftwareApplication` + `FAQPage` + optional `HowTo` (`#setup-steps`) + `ItemList` (`#audience`) |
| **API marketing hub / platform** | `CollectionPage` or `WebPage` + `SoftwareApplication` + `ItemList` + `HowTo` (`#setup-steps`) + `WebPage` (`#pricing` offers) + `ItemList` (`#audience`) + `FAQPage` |
| **Tool pages** | `WebApplication` (+ `WebSite` `isPartOf` on channel routes) |
| **Blog / post preview** | `BlogPosting` or `SocialMediaPosting` + `BreadcrumbList` (+ `FAQPage` / `HowTo` / `Product` with a free `Offer`) + optional `SoftwareSourceCode` via `BlogPosting.hasPart` |
| **Docs article** | `TechArticle` + `BreadcrumbList` (+ optional `HowTo` from `<Steps>`) + `ImageObject` + `SoftwareSourceCode` via `TechArticle.hasPart` (fenced markdown + OpenAPI client samples when load-time spec fetch succeeds) |
| **Blog hubs** | `Blog` + `CollectionPage` + `ItemList` (index); `ProfilePage` + `Person` (author); topic `CollectionPage` + breadcrumbs |
| **Creator profile** | `ProfilePage` + `Person` |
| **Playbook / building block detail** | `WebPage` + `Person` + `HowTo` / `CreativeWork` / merged CMS schema |
| **Compare** | `WebPage` + `ItemList` + `SoftwareApplication` × 2 + `FAQPage` |
| **Alternatives hub** | `CollectionPage` + `ItemList` |
| **Alternatives detail** | `WebPage` + `ItemList` + `SoftwareApplication` × N + `FAQPage` (OpenQuok node: `isAccessibleForFree` + free `Offer`) |

## Builder notes

### FAQPage (`createPublicFaqSEOSchema`)

- `pageUrl: \`${canonical}#faq\`` — same section name/description as visible `PublicFaq`.
- Plain-text `Answer.text` matching accordion copy (HTML answers: `prepareBlogRichTextForDisplay` then `stripHtmlToPlainText`; link labels kept).
- Returns `{}` when empty — always `filterNonEmptyJsonLdNodes`.

### HowTo setup steps (`createPublicSetupStepsSEOSchema`)

- Maps visible **`FeaturesOrdered`** sections to [`HowTo`](https://schema.org/HowTo) at `{canonical}#setup-steps`.
- `sectionTitle` → `name` (comma spacing normalized like hero titles); `sectionDescription` or `sectionSubtitle` → `description`; each step `title` / `content` → `HowToStep.name` / `HowToStep.text` (plain text only — no terminal mock HTML).
- Wired from agent/MCP landing loads (`agentVm.setupSteps*`) and API marketing loads (`getPublicApiHubSetupStepsSection` / `getPublicApiPlatformSetupStepsSection`). MCP pages SSR **both** `#setup-steps` (MCP tab) and `#skill-setup-steps` (skill tab) via `buildPublicMcpSetupStepsSeoSchemas`.
- Returns `{}` when `steps` is empty or `sectionTitle` is missing — always `filterNonEmptyJsonLdNodes`.
- Underlying helper: `createHowToSEOSchema` (also used by docs `<Steps>` and blog CMS how-to fields).

### Pricing offers (`createPublicPricingSEOSchema`)

- Paid tiers from `GetPublicPricingPresenter` + **`$0` self-host** from `PUBLIC_SELF_HOST_PRICING_FOOTNOTE_CONFIG` in `publicSelfHostingLandingConfig.ts` (same copy as `PublicSelfHostPricingFootnote.svelte`).
- **`/pricing`**: attach full offer list to the main `WebPage` node.
- **Home + API marketing** (`PublicMarketingPricingSection`): emit `WebPage` at `{canonical}#pricing` — visible section uses `id="pricing"` on `PublicPricingTabs`.
- **`/self-hosting`**: single self-host `Offer` via `createPublicSelfHostPricingOffer`.
- Helpers: `createPublicPricingOffers`, `createPublicPaidPlanOffers`, `createPublicSelfHostPricingOffer`, `createPublicPricingSectionSEOSchema`. Always `filterNonEmptyJsonLdNodes`.

### VideoObject (`createLandingDemoSEOSchema`)

- Landing demo from SSR `landing_page` config. Filter when `youtubeVideoId` or `uploadDate` is empty.
- Include `uploadDate` (ISO 8601) — required by Google for VideoObject rich results (`DEMO_YOUTUBE_UPLOAD_DATE`).
- `HeroDemo`: crawlable thumbnail, YouTube link, `id="landing-demo"`.

### Organization (`createOrganizationSEOSchema`)

- Landing and about only — not sitewide. Use `organizationSchemaId(origin)` for stable `@id`.

### Product (`createBlogPostSEOSchema`)

Google Product snippets require **`offers`**, **`review`**, or **`aggregateRating`**. Blog product JSON-LD always includes a free `Offer` (`price: '0'`, `priceCurrency: 'USD'`, `availability: InStock`) — same as public tool `WebApplication` nodes. Do not emit a bare `Product` with only name/description/brand.

### Docs code snippets (`createDocsPageSeoSchema` + `createSoftwareSourceCodeNodes`)

- **`buildDocsPageLoadExtras`** parses raw markdown (`extractDocsCodeBlocksFromRaw`) and, when frontmatter includes **`openapi:`**, best-effort merges static HTTP client samples from **`fetchOpenapiOperationForDocs`** (cURL, Python, JavaScript, PHP, Go, Java, Ruby). Omit OpenAPI blocks when the spec fetch fails so prerender does not break.
- **`createDocsPageSeoSchema`** sets **`TechArticle.hasPart`** to `@id` refs of each **`SoftwareSourceCode`** node (same pattern as **`BlogPosting.hasPart`** for blog posts). Author on doc code nodes is **`Organization`** (site title + origin), not **`Person`**.
- Wired from docs **`+page.ts`** loads → **`DocsSeoHead.svelte`**. Extraction uses raw markdown, not rendered HTML.

## Canonical alignment

JSON-LD `url` / `canonicalUrl` must match `<link rel="canonical">` — use the same `buildCanonicalUrl(url)` value (see **web-seo-canonical**). Do not duplicate title/description in `+page.svelte` when they already exist in the server load.
